      {
        "id": "inherited-boolean-shape-threshold",
        "origin": "authoring_observation",
        "status": "suspected",
        "classification": "defect",
        "description": "The unchanged automatic shape selector carries its Boolean threshold defect into multi-GEMM.",
        "trigger": "Automatic Hopper/Blackwell selection with bits<=6 and n<=4096, for example bits=3, k=16384 and n=4096.",
        "expected_behavior": "A dimensional threshold should distinguish qualifying dimensions; the precise intended replacement condition is not established.",
        "actual_behavior": "(size_k && bits >= 3) is Boolean and cannot exceed 8192, so this branch always returns shape 2. Parent-tree search identifies the existing select_exl3_gemm_kernel caller; the task adds select_exl3_mgemm_kernel as another direct caller. Positive forced shape indices bypass the expression.",
